   "narration": {
    "en": "The -ed ending has three sounds. After t or d it is pronounced /id/, as in waited and heeded. After voiceless sounds like p, k and s it is /t/, and after most other sounds it is /d/, as in whispered and offered. An adjective like aged or ragged."
